    "updated_at": "2025-04-16T21:55:58Z",
    "body": "From the [last meeting](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11109), there was a desire to bring back the `interesttarget` [touchscreen behavior issue](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11058) for another discussion. The last meeting's minutes are [here](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11058#issuecomment-2740976896), for reference, but it was mentioned that a few folks (@hober, @annevk, and @martinthomson) made comments on the [issue](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11058#issuecomment-2696424647), but weren't able to make [Meeting #18](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11109) for the discussion. Those folks should have a chance to directly represent those opinions, so we can discuss them live and understand them better. Hopefully those folks can make this meeting time? I know that's tough geographically, so if there's a better time of day, we can also try to schedule a special breakout session on this topic. Please let me know!",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
